<%
  // locals: lastReviewed (build month, e.g. "October 2026"), site, stamp, links.
-%>
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <%- include('sections/head') %>
  </head>
  <body class="page-static">
    <%- include('sections/header') %>
    <main id="main">
      <div class="container static-page">
        <p class="static-page__label">Legal</p>
        <h1 class="static-page__title">Privacy Notice</h1>
        <div class="doc">
          <p><em>Last reviewed: <%= lastReviewed %></em></p>

          <h2>Summary</h2>
          <p>I do not collect, store, or process any personal data directly. This website uses a small number of third-party services that may process your IP address as part of normal web operation. No analytics or tracking are performed.</p>

          <h2>Who I am</h2>
          <p>
            CodesThings.com is the personal website of James Macmillan.<br />
            Contact: <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a>
          </p>

          <h2>What data is processed and by whom</h2>
          <p>I do not directly collect or store personal data. The following third-party services are used to operate the site and may process your IP address:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>GitHub Pages</strong>: hosts this website. GitHub may log IP addresses per their <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Privacy Statement</a>.</li>
            <li><strong>YouTube</strong>: the ZeroCalc blog post shows a video. Until you click it, the post shows a plain link and your browser makes no request to YouTube. If you click to play, the video loads from <code>youtube-nocookie.com</code>, YouTube's privacy-enhanced embed, and Google may process your IP address per their <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Privacy Policy</a>.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>Fonts, icons and scripts are all served from this site. The source code for this website is publicly available at <a href="https://github.com/jamescodesthings/jamescodesthings.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">github.com/jamescodesthings/jamescodesthings.github.io</a>.</p>

          <h2>Legal basis</h2>
          <p>Third-party service processing described above is carried out on the basis of legitimate interests in operating a functional, accessible website (UK GDPR Article 6(1)(f)).</p>

          <h2>Cookies and local storage</h2>
          <p>This site sets no cookies. It stores the following items on your device, in your browser's <code>localStorage</code> or <code>sessionStorage</code>. They never leave your device. More detail is on the <a href="/about-cookies">About Cookies</a> page.</p>
          <%- include('sections/storage-keys') %>

          <h2>Your rights</h2>
          <p>Under UK GDPR you have the right to: access your personal data; rectification of inaccurate data; erasure; restriction of processing; data portability; and to object to processing. To exercise rights relating to third-party processing, please contact those services directly.</p>

          <h2>Right to complain</h2>
          <p>You have the right to lodge a complaint with the <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Information Commissioner's Office (ICO)</a> if you believe your data has been handled unlawfully.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </main>
    <%- include('sections/footer') %>
    <script type="module" src="/js/main.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
